    return 1;
}
# ⛔ 6.7.17 (D108, the user's decision, 2026-10-22: "refuse it naming the array of vectors, as D103") — AN UNTYPED
# DECLARATION FROM AN ARRAY OF VECTORS IS REFUSED. `var wa: f64v2[2]; var x = wa;` bound one word, element 0's lane 0
# (exit 4 with wa[0] = (4, 7)), in a fn and at top level (`var X = GA;`), on every target, where D103 refuses the same
# name in every word slot and D95 copies a vector (an array is no vector to copy). In a fn, PARSE_VAR's untyped
# declaration (cursor on the `=`, `_vin_avv`); at top level, the zone and after the first statement (`_vtop_vval`):
# the whole initialiser an array of vectors (`_vval_at`, `_vvl_arr`) — "'wa' is an array of vectors - an untyped
